The first construction failed honestly: the exact brancher solved the shipping instance in 16 nodes, and greedy solved 7/8 seeds. The issue was excessive planted incidence—two forced plant neighbors per decoy made small dominating sets easy. A one-neighbor, degree-balanced regime is materially harder in the initial sweep; I’m measuring it against the full eight-seed panel now rather than weakening the attack.
