+bipartition.  Edges between the two selected halves are forbidden.  Each
+unselected vertex receives plant_degree random neighbors in the selected
+opposite half, certifying domination.  Noise edges between the two unselected
+halves are sampled at a probability chosen to equalise expected planted and
+decoy degrees.  All public labels are then uniformly permuted.  The certificate
+is known by inverse generation and Lemma 4; no instance is solved.
+
