    Let $U^* \subseteq V(G)$ be the unique minimum vertex cover of $G$ such that $\tilde{U} \subseteq U^*$.
    Observe that $N(v) \setminus U^* \neq \emptyset$ for $v \in U^*$.
    This follows from the fact that if $N(v) \subseteq U^*$, $U^* \setminus \{v\}$ is also a vertex cover of $G$, which contradicts the minimality of $U^*$.
