The first hardening idea also failed: exact biregularity with one planted neighbor creates pairwise-disjoint neighborhoods, and a 30-line compatibility-clique attack recovers every shipping witness in about a millisecond. I’m replacing that leakage with a truly degree-regular conditioned model whose decoys have a randomized mix of one and two planted neighbors, then testing the generic, spectral, set-cover, codegree, and exact-search routes before deciding whether Track A is supportable.
